[size=5]Cartur's Blacksmithing[/size]

More from the Crafting skill you already have, for weapons and armour. Gear you forge lasts longer, you count as extra workbench and forge upgrades, at 70 you repair from your bag, and at 80 your gear takes one more upgrade.

Inspired by [b]Smoothbrain's Blacksmithing[/b] (retired in 2026), by Smoothbrain and [url=https://github.com/blaxxun-boop/Blacksmithing]blaxxun-boop[/url] - credit to them for the idea and the design. This is a separate mod written for Valheim 1.0.

[size=4]What it does[/size]

Valheim 1.0 has a Crafting skill of its own - it rises as you craft, repair and build. Everything here builds on it, so there is no second skill to grind.

[list]
[*][b]Any level[/b] - weapons and armour you craft last longer, double durability at 100. An upgrade keeps the higher smith level.
[*][b]Level 10 / 20[/b] - you count as one / two extra workbench upgrades.
[*][b]Level 30 / 40[/b] - one / two extra forge upgrades.
[*][b]Level 50 / 60[/b] - one / two extra black forge and galdr table upgrades.
[*][b]Level 70[/b] - repair your gear from the inventory, no station needed.
[*][b]Level 80[/b] - weapons and armour take one upgrade past their normal maximum, at 3x the materials.
[/list]

Every level can be changed or turned off in the config.

[size=4]Multiplayer[/size]

Install it on the server too and its numbers apply to everyone.

Source: [url=https://github.com/jekkle/cartur-blacksmithing]github.com/jekkle/cartur-blacksmithing[/url]

